gator Support\nSponsors\nVeterinarians (rDVMs)\nSupport the BBVCTO\nReferring Veterinarians\nResources\nAbout\nBack to Main Menu\nAbout\nAbout Overview\nCareers\nCollege of Veterinary Medicine\nLocations\nGiving\nEmergency\nI am a...\nToggles the 'I am a' Menu with links to the OSU Veterinary Medical Center and the College of Veterinary Medicine\nI am a...\nToggles the 'I am a' Menu with links to the OSU Veterinary Medical Center and the College of Veterinary Medicine\nVeterinary Medical Center\nCompanion Animal Owner\nCompanion Animal Services\nHummel & Trueman Hospital for Companion Animals\nFrank Stanton Veterinary Spectrum of Care Clinic\nVeterinary Medical Center at Dublin\nClinical Trials\nFarm Animal or Horse Owner\nFarm Animal Services\nHospital for Farm Animal\nLarge Animal Services at Marysville\nEquine Services\nGalbreath Equine Center\nReferring Veterinarian\nReferring Veterinarian Portal\nPartnering With You\nClinical Trials\nJob Seeker\nCareers\nAbout the VMC\nContact Us\nCollege of Veterinary Medicine\nProspective Student\nAcademic Programs\nFinancial Aid\nBuckeye Vet Camp\nMiddle School and High School Prep\nResidency Programs\nCurrent Student\nFinancial Aid\nClass Schedule\nAcademic Programs\nVeterinary Student Research Opportunities\nCollege Research Day\nHealth and Wellbeing Resources\nAlumni or Friend\nAlumni Section\nAlumni Society\nGet Involved\nGiving\nContinuing Education\nResearcher\nSignature Programs\nGrant Support\nEnvironmental Health and Safety\nVeterinary Bioscience Services\nFaculty or Staff Member\nHR.OSU.EDU\nCVM Community\nHealth and Wellbeing Resources\nVIS - Veterinary Information Systems\nWorkday\nCompanion Animal Owner\nBack\nCompanion Animal Owner\nCompanion Animal Services\nHummel & Trueman Hospital for Companion Animals\nFrank Stanton Veterinary Spectrum of Care Clinic\nVeterinary Medical Center at Dublin\nClinical Trials\nFarm Animal or Horse Owner\nBack\nFarm Animal or Horse Owner\nFarm Animal Services\nHospital for Farm Animal\nLarge Animal Services at Marysville\nEquine Services\nGalbreath Equine Center\nReferring Veterinarian\nBack\nReferring Veterinarian\nReferring Veterinarian Portal\nPartnering With You\nClinical Trials\nJob Seeker\nBack\nJob Seeker\nCareers\nAbout the VMC\nContact Us\nBuckeyeLink\nFind People\nWebmail\nSearch Ohio State\nClose Emergency Menu\nNeed immediate care?\nCompanion\nEmergency\n(614) 889-8070\nVeterinary Medical Center at Dublin\nAfter-hours urgent care\nEquine\nEmergency\n(614) 292-6661\nGalbreath Equine Center & Ralph Rogan Equine Performance Evaluation Arena\n24 hours / 7 days a week\nFarm\nEmergency\n(614) 292-6661\nHospital for Farm Animals\n24 hours / 7 days a week\nCompanion\nEmergency\n(614) 292-3551\nHummel Trueman Hospital for Companion Animals\nOpen 24 hours\nEquine\nFarm\nEmergency\n(937) 642-2936\nLarge Animal Services at Marysville\n24 hours / 7 days a week\nLearn more about all of our emergency, urgent, and critical care services\nImmunotherapy for canine oral melanoma\nImmunotherapy for canine oral melanoma\nOral melanoma is a highly aggressive disease with poor outcomes and no effective treatments. Our recent research has shown that a weakened form of the lymphocytic choriomeningitis virus (LCMV) is safe, and can trigger strong anti-tumor effects.\nBy injecting a small amount of this weakened virus directly into the tumor, we aim to activate the dog's immune system to fight the cancer. Additionally, we will collect and expand immune cells from the tumor, as these cells are more likely to recognize and attack cancer cells. These enhanced immune cells will then be reinfused into the patient to target existing or potential metastatic disease.\nTo evaluate our therapy, we will first perform a tumor biopsy to confirm the diagnosis and analyze the immune cells already present (Tumor-infiltrating lymphocytes). We will then inject the tumor with the weakened virus. One week later, the tumor will be surgically removed, and immune cells from the cancer will be expanded for future use if metastases are present or develop later. After treatment, we will closely monitor the patients through periodic blood tests and imaging (CT scans) every three months.\nA small group of dogs (randomly selected) will be the control, and while not receiving the virus injection, they will have their immune cells extracted from the tumor and expanded to be reinfused in case of progressive disease.\nClient Compensation:\nCost of tumor biopsy, two CT imaging sessions, trial-related blood work, the viral reagent and injections, the collection priming and reinjection of the immune cells. Additionally, participating dogs are eligible to receive a $800 post-trial incentive.\nPotential Medical Benefits:\nPotential medical benefits include longer clinical remissions after surgical removal of the primary tumor, slowing down or remission of metastatic disease.\nPotential Medical Risks:\nFollowing tumor biopsy: bleeding, infection of the tumor, swelling, redness, pain, fever, and/or discharge/pus/odor at the biopsy site.\nFollowing virus injection and reinfusion of immune cells, skin rash, fever, lethargy, and anaphylaxis.\nWhat qualifies my pet for enrollment?\nInclusion Criteria:\nDogs that are otherwise healthy with localized cytologically or histologically confirmed oral melanoma will be recruited to the study.\nTumors need to be easily accessible to percutaneous injection and needle biopsy.\nExclusion Criteria:\nDogs with a history of immune deficiency or requiring immunosuppressive medications will be excluded.\nA dog that received local radiation therapy to the primary tumor before trial enrolment will be excluded.\nDiagnosis/Condition Being Studied:\nOral melanoma\nIntervention to Be Studied:\nInjection of weakened virus into the tumor and transfusion of tumor-infiltrating lymphocytes\nDownload PDF\nPRE-SCREENING QUESTIONAIRE\nIf you believe your pet may be eligible for this study, please complete a pre-screening questionnaire.\nPre-Screen Here\nPre-Screen Here\nContact:\nEmail:\nCVM-ClinicalTrials@osu.edu\nThe Ohio State University\nVeterinary Medical Center Facebook Page\nVeterinary Medical Center Instagram Page\nVeterinary Medical Center Twitter Page\nVeterinary Medical Center LinkedIn Page\nVeterinary Medical Center YouTube Page\nVeterinary Medical Center at Dublin\n5020 Bradenton Avenue\nDublin 43017 OH\n(614) 889-8070\nFrank Stanton Veterinary Spectrum of Care Clinic\n655 Vernon L. Tharp St\nColumbus 43210 OH\n(614) 292-1573\nGalbreath Equine Center & Ralph Rogan Equine Performance Evaluation Arena\n685 Vernon L. Tharp Street\nColumbus 43210 OH\n(614) 292-6661\nHospital for Farm Animals\n601 Vernon L. Tharp St\nColumbus 43210 OH\n(614) 292-6661\nHummel Trueman Hospital for Companion Animals\n601 Vernon L. Tharp Street\nColumbus 43210 OH\n(614) 292-3551\nLarge Animal Services at Marysville\n16410 County Home Rd\nMarysville 43040 OH\n(937) 642-2936\nHelpful Links\nCareers\nContact Us\nPay My Bill\nReferring Vets Portal\nVeterinary Medical Center Facebook Page\nVeterinary Medical Center Instagram Page\nVeterinary Medical Center Twitter Page\nVeterinary Medical Center LinkedIn Page\nVeterinary Medical Center YouTube Page\nLooking for the College of Veterinary Medicine?\nPlease Visit\nvet.osu.edu\nPlease Call\n(614) 292-1171\nNon-discrimination Notice\nPrivacy Statement\nCookie Settings\n©\n2026\nThe Ohio State University\nIf you have a disability and experience difficulty accessing this content, contact\nCVM-DigitalAccessibility@osu.edu",
